<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-16351] C++ thin and ODBC: SSL keystore shouldn&apos;t be a mandatory parameter</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-16351</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Currently, SSL in C++ thin client and ODBC can&apos;t be configured without specifying client-side certificates. This shouldn&apos;t be the case - SSL can be used without any corticates or custom trust stores on the client.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Need to add a way to do this out of the box.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
